{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-26T19:02:10.791Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9a3d0027739dfadbcc41b040","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1606"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1606: Validate public SDK runtime operand values before mutation internals"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"**Version:** `@unbrained/pm-cli` 2026.10.26 SDK (`@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk`), Node 24.19.0.\n\n**Repro** (`node --experimental-strip-types x.ts`):\n```ts\nimport { PmClient } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk';\nconst pm = new PmClient({ pmRoot: '.agents/pm', author: 'agent' });\nawait pm.append('pm-xxxx', { text: 'object not string' } as any);\n```\n**Observed:** uncaught `TypeError: a.trim is not a function` with a minified bundle excerpt — 7,414 bytes of stderr, no error code, and nothing naming `append`'s body operand. Catching it yields only the bare TypeError. Updating with a numeric `estimatedMinutes: 2` likewise throws `TypeError: e.trim is not a function` (the string `'2'` works).\n\n**Expected:** public SDK methods validate positional/option value types at the boundary and throw a typed `PmCliError` (usage code) naming the operand, the expected type and a short corrective example (e.g. \"append body must be a string; use comments(id, { add }) for a comment\").\n\n**Why it matters for agents:** agents and tool/JSON bridges call the SDK with dynamically built values, so TypeScript types do not protect them. A minified TypeError forces the agent to inspect bundled internals to fix a simple call-shape mistake. (Related but different: #1520 is about unknown option keys being dropped.)\n\n\nIntake boundary: this is a report against published 2026.10.26, not proof of a current-checkout defect. Reproduce in an external sandbox before implementation. Related completed work retains its shipped scope. Proposed examples or categories are not accepted contracts until validated.\n\nSource: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1606"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","github","sdk"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-26T19:02:10.791Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-26T19:02:10.791Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Native public-client controls cover an object append operand and numeric estimatedMinutes according to the published input contract, alongside valid corresponding values.; Errors identify the public method, operand, expected type and corrective example through PmCliError usage semantics; rejected calls leave documents, history and receipts unchanged.; Validation derives from SDK-owned contracts across convenience methods and JSON bridges, preserving completed unknown-key and bulk-duration guards without mirrored per-wrapper schemas or a global exception handler."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-9rgaal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Invalid runtime operand values produce typed field-specific usage errors before any write, while valid public SDK inputs and custom project fields retain their documented semantics."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-bulk-option-validation","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-26T19:02:10.791Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-fl3phm","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-26T19:02:10.791Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:02:10.791Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check: fresh orientation, request-specific search, open/in-progress inventories and complete strict 3126-item all-status corpus found no open owner for this exact case. Full live metadata and histories of related owners confirm their completed, distinct scope. This is intake only, open and unclaimed; implementation is outside the current delivery cohort."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"b896c65b2a9b3b4ec91211b7cc26d4fe49915b4e4d1fe957219dd46a2353d28e","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"fdf6fcc0f0b3c7f49ac82e8f1d69c9fe2abbdef1d9262e365ba9494ad44c90c0"}
